o die that he was  sorry to me and my sister for making us  worry and that's the sort of guy that i  lost  he died after 42 nights on a ventilator  in a coma  me and my sister were allowed in for his  final moments we could only touch him  through ppe  and he was completely unconscious so he  had no idea that we were there when we  let them turn his ventilator down and  watched him die  i will for those to be the last words he  said yeah good man your dad a good man  but  so it happens on the 20th of may where  we now learn the prime minister was in  attendance and whatever you want to call  was going on in the back gardens of  number 10 but but he was there on that  day you were you were  applying for your father's death  certificate  yeah we um were getting his death  certificate signed um the only thing on  there was covered because he had no  underlying health conditions  we were um  shopping for a care package for his icu  nurses because speaking to them on the  phone for those 42 nights we could tell  they were not taking care of themselves  they also asked us for amazon vouchers  from donations we got in dad's name  because they had no ppe and that's the  only way they were buying it  so why families like mine grieving  families  were bereaved were alone away from their  loved ones and their friends having lost  a guy like dad  orris johnson spent 25 minutes at a  garden party where 100 people have been  invited to bring their own booze and  enjoy the weather  you met him  at dining street before of course all of  this this emerged i mean what was the  the nature of your discussion what did  the prime minister say to you in in that  garden  so i met him in the exact same garden  where he'd hosted this party on the 20th  of may the year before which to me seems  callous and cruel to host bereaved  people in the same garden  and i met him i told him my dad's story  and i showed him a picture of my dad on  a ventilator which i'd never shown to  anybody before  h